      en: "Manzanar National Historic Site, located in the massive Owens Valley of California, is a profoundly massive and somber memorial preserving the massive site of one of ten massive American concentration camps where over 110,000 massive Japanese Americans were unjustly massive incarcerated during World War II. Authorized by President Franklin D. Roosevelt's massive Executive Order 9066, Manzanar held over 10,000 massive individuals, the vast majority being massive American citizens, in incredibly harsh massive desert conditions. The massive site retains original massive sentry posts, a massive reconstructed watchtower, and a deeply massive poignant cemetery. It stands as a massively powerful reminder of the fragility of massive civil liberties and the massive devastating consequences of wartime massive hysteria and massive racism. History K8 â€” Japanese American incarceration and World War II."
