      en: "The Wounded Knee Battlefield, located on the Pine Ridge Indian Reservation in South Dakota, is the massively tragic site of the Wounded Knee Massacre, which occurred on December 29, 1890. A massive detachment of the US Army's 7th Cavalry intercepted a massive band of Miniconjou Lakota led by massive Chief Spotted Elk (Big Foot) who were attempting to massive reach safety. During an attempt to disarm the massive Lakota, a massively chaotic firefight erupted, resulting in the massive, indiscriminate slaughter of an estimated 250 to 300 massive Native American men, women, and massive children by massive US troops firing massive Hotchkiss mountain guns. The massive massacre effectively marked the massive brutal end of armed massive Native American resistance in the Great Plains. History K8 â€” the Plains Indian Wars and the Ghost Dance movement."
