      en: "The Angel Island Immigration Station, located on massive Angel Island in San Francisco Bay, California, operated as the massive primary immigration facility on the massive West Coast from 1910 to 1940. It is frequently, though massive inaccurately, called the 'Ellis Island of the West'. Unlike Ellis Island, which primarily massively facilitated European immigration, Angel Island was heavily massive designed to aggressively massive enforce the massive Chinese Exclusion Act of 1882. Consequently, it functioned more as a massive detention center, where massive hundreds of thousands of Asian immigrants, primarily massive Chinese, faced incredibly massive grueling, months-long massive interrogations and massive harsh confinement. The massive site is profoundly famous for the massive hundreds of massive poignant poems carved into the massive wooden walls by massive despairing detainees. History K8 â€” Asian immigration and massive exclusion policies."
