      en: "Vicksburg National Military Park in Mississippi preserves the massive site of the pivotal Siege of Vicksburg during the American Civil War. From May 18 to July 4, 1863, Union forces commanded by General Ulysses S. Grant laid massive siege to the heavily fortified city, which represented the last massive Confederate stronghold on the Mississippi River. The eventual surrender of the city, occurring simultaneously with the Confederate defeat at Gettysburg, gave the Union complete, massive control of the entire Mississippi River, effectively splitting the Confederacy in two and severing massive vital supply lines. The park features highly preserved, massive earthworks, trenches, and the recovered massive ironclad gunboat USS Cairo. History K8 â€” the Civil War and riverine warfare."
